  "reading": {
   "title": "Hafsa's healthy habits",
   "text": "Hafsa wants to be healthy and strong, so she has some good habits. She always drinks a big glass of water when she wakes up. She usually eats fruit for breakfast, and she often eats vegetables with lunch and dinner. She rarely eats sugar, but she sometimes has a small piece of Turkish delight with her tea.\n\nEvery day, she walks for thirty minutes in the park. On Mondays and Thursdays, she stretches and does some exercise at home. Her neighbor Linda goes to the gym twice a week, and she asks Hafsa to come. Hafsa says, \"Maybe next month!\"\n\nHer son Emre is different. He never eats vegetables, and he often wants candy. Hafsa is not angry. Every evening, she makes a healthy snack, and Emre usually eats it. She says, \"A good diet gives energy, and energy is important for school.\"",
